     "heading": {
      "zh-Hant": "馬來亞戰役中的所屬部隊",
      "en": "The Malayan campaign"
     },
     "body": {
      "zh-Hant": "1941年3月4日，辛格隨所屬營調往馬來亞。日軍入侵後，他所在的營在吉打州日得拉被擊潰；駐馬來亞半島北部的英軍包括他的第1營第14旁遮普團，向南撤退，他本人帶著部分士兵成為散兵，在尋找主力部隊。1941年12月中旬，他在阿羅士打附近與日方藤原小組接觸並投降。吉隆坡於1942年1月11日陷落，新加坡於2月15日陷落。辛格在這場馬來亞戰役中由一名營級軍官轉為戰俘的收容者，這成為他其後籌組印度國民軍的起點。",
      "en": "Mohan Singh was posted out to Malaya with his unit on 4 March 1941. After the Japanese invasion his battalion was overpowered at Jitra in Kedah; the British force in the northern part of the Malay Peninsula, including his 1/14 Punjab Regiment, fled south, and he, with some of his men, became a straggler in search of the main body. Around the middle of December 1941 he contacted Major Fujiwara's group near Alor Star and surrendered. Kuala Lumpur fell on 11 January 1942 and Singapore on 15 February. In this Malayan campaign he passed from battalion officer to custodian of the prisoners of war, the starting point of his later formation of the Indian National Army."
     },
